{
 "summary": "Checkout 502s start in inventory, not the gateway. Inventory logs 'connection pool exhausted' and returns 500 on POST /reserve. Orders and gateway pass that up as 502s, and all three log patterns share the same example trace IDs. The gateway 1.5.3 deploy at 09:13:13Z came about 30s before the errors, but nothing in the evidence ties gateway code to the failure.",
 "root_cause": {
  "statement": "Inventory's connection pool is exhausted, so POST /reserve returns 500. Orders and then gateway propagate it as 502 on checkout.",
  "service": "inventory",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "evidence_ids": [
   "ev-23d4c2b9c411",
   "ev-97ec8dd1752c",
   "ev-2bbdc45c9d49",
   "ev-b07f2f336800",
   "ev-4df59038eeb9"
  ]
 },
 "contributing_factors": [
  {
   "statement": "Inventory's 5xx ratio (avg 18.9%, max 50%) matches orders' and is higher than gateway's, which fits inventory being where errors begin.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-4df59038eeb9",
    "ev-c5447ed2471d",
    "ev-6d5399d5f26e"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Failures are fast (7-20ms) and p95 latency stayed flat in every service. This is fail-fast pool exhaustion, not a timeout cascade.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-97ec8dd1752c",
    "ev-4df59038eeb9",
    "ev-6d5399d5f26e"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "timeline": [
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T09:13:13Z",
   "event": "gateway deployed 1.4.2 -> 1.5.3",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-17ee17817f45"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T09:13:45Z",
   "event": "inventory begins logging 'connection pool exhausted'; orders and gateway log matching errors for the same traces",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-23d4c2b9c411",
    "ev-2bbdc45c9d49",
    "ev-b07f2f336800"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T09:14:12Z",
   "event": "5xx ratio crosses 5% on gateway, orders and inventory",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-6d5399d5f26e",
    "ev-c5447ed2471d",
    "ev-4df59038eeb9"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T09:15:42Z",
   "event": "Sampled error traces show gateway 502 <- orders 502 <- inventory 500",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-97ec8dd1752c"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "ruled_out": [
  {
   "statement": "A gateway 1.5.3 code defect is unlikely to be the direct cause. Gateway errors only quote 'orders returned 502', and the deepest failing span is inventory POST /reserve (500) with a pool-exhaustion log.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-b07f2f336800",
    "ev-97ec8dd1752c",
    "ev-23d4c2b9c411",
    "ev-17ee17817f45"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Latency or timeout saturation is unlikely: p95 stays low and failing traces finish in 7-20ms.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-97ec8dd1752c",
    "ev-6d5399d5f26e",
    "ev-4df59038eeb9",
    "ev-c5447ed2471d"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "unknowns": [
  "Whether the gateway 1.5.3 deploy indirectly caused inventory pool exhaustion, for example by changing retries, concurrency or connection reuse. Request rates look modest (~1.5 rps to inventory), and no pre-deploy baseline is in the snapshot.",
  "Which pool is exhausted in inventory (DB or downstream HTTP), and its size and current usage. No pool or DB metrics were collected.",
  "No deployment records for inventory or orders, so a recent change there can't be confirmed or excluded.",
  "Whether inventory errors existed before 09:13:13Z, which would separate this from the gateway deploy."
 ],
 "recommended_actions": [
  {
   "action": "Investigate inventory's connection pool: active and idle connections, pool size, the database or backend it connects to, and any leaked or long-held connections. Restart or scale inventory, or raise the pool limit, as mitigation.",
   "rationale": "Inventory is the deepest failing span and logs 'connection pool exhausted' for the same traces that fail upstream.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-23d4c2b9c411",
    "ev-97ec8dd1752c"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Compare gateway 1.5.3 with 1.4.2 for changes in retries, concurrency or call patterns to orders and inventory, and roll gateway back to 1.4.2 if that's cheap.",
   "rationale": "The deploy came about 30s before the errors. That timing is a lead, but no evidence ties gateway code to the failure.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-17ee17817f45",
    "ev-b07f2f336800"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Pull deployment and config change history for inventory and orders, plus pre-09:13 error metrics.",
   "rationale": "This would confirm or rule out a change on the inventory side and set a baseline.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-4df59038eeb9"
   ]
  }
 ]
}
